      "writtenOn": "2022-04-29T22:08:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have not encountered this case, but if a process is TASK_UNINTERRUPTIBLE then it should never return from the kernel if it is frozen and then a kill is attempted. Whenever the process would have normally returned to userspace, the freezer will prevent that and the process should also have a lovely pending kill signal waiting to be handled.\n\nThe act of initially freezing such a process should do essentially nothing at all. See the Optimizations section here: https://blogs.oracle.com/linux/post/freezing-tasks-ksplice",
      "parentUuid": "12c12afd_b77fcc2a",
      "revId": "c24b094ead69bfe8ca01c38f602fba9d2ed97077",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
